WEBVTT

1
00:00:39,841 --> 00:00:46,046
[sinister music playing]

2
00:00:54,154 --> 00:00:57,157
[thunder roaring]

3
00:00:58,960 --> 00:01:01,896
[thunder roaring]

4
00:01:01,963 --> 00:01:04,599
[fire crackling]

5
00:01:04,666 --> 00:01:06,501
[distinct screams]

6
00:01:09,136 --> 00:01:10,470
Help!

7
00:01:13,206 --> 00:01:15,510
No! Please, no!

8
00:01:17,210 --> 00:01:19,379
Please, no!

9
00:01:20,815 --> 00:01:22,349
[Sarah screams]

10
00:01:25,787 --> 00:01:31,793
[soft music playing]

11
00:01:36,564 --> 00:01:41,936
<i>♪ It will joy</i>
<i>and comfort give you ♪</i>

12
00:01:42,003 --> 00:01:47,041
<i>♪ Take it then</i>
<i>wherever you go ♪</i>

13
00:01:47,174 --> 00:01:49,844
<i>-♪ Precious name ♪</i>
<i>-♪ Precious name ♪</i>

14
00:01:49,911 --> 00:01:52,780
<i>-♪ Oh, how sweet ♪</i>
<i>-♪ Oh, how sweet ♪</i>

15
00:01:52,847 --> 00:01:58,452
<i>♪ Hope of Earth</i>
<i>and joy of Heav'n ♪</i>

16
00:01:58,519 --> 00:02:01,022
<i>-♪ Precious name ♪</i>
<i>-♪ Precious name ♪</i>

17
00:02:01,089 --> 00:02:03,658
<i>-♪ Oh, how sweet ♪</i>
<i>-♪ Oh, how sweet ♪</i>

18
00:02:03,725 --> 00:02:05,059
[coughs]

19
00:02:05,192 --> 00:02:09,831
<i>♪ Hope of Earth</i>
<i>and joy of Heav'n... ♪</i>

20
00:02:12,600 --> 00:02:15,903
That's beautiful. What is it?

21
00:02:15,970 --> 00:02:18,205
Sarah's favorite.

22
00:02:18,205 --> 00:02:20,240
She'd climb up
on the dining room table

23
00:02:20,307 --> 00:02:23,443
and sing that hymn
every time we had guests.

24
00:02:23,511 --> 00:02:25,513
Oh.

25
00:02:25,580 --> 00:02:28,583
[coughs]

26
00:02:30,084 --> 00:02:31,119
Here you are.

27
00:02:31,218 --> 00:02:33,220
Oh, thank you.

28
00:02:34,088 --> 00:02:35,123
Julia.

29
00:02:35,222 --> 00:02:36,524
Right.

30
00:02:37,892 --> 00:02:39,927
Um, are those my keys?

31
00:02:39,994 --> 00:02:41,361
No.

32
00:02:41,428 --> 00:02:43,031
Evelyn.
I keep mace on there.

33
00:02:43,097 --> 00:02:44,464
They're mine.
No.

34
00:02:44,532 --> 00:02:47,769
I wouldn't want you
hurting yourself.

35
00:02:47,835 --> 00:02:49,302
What?

36
00:02:50,237 --> 00:02:51,973
Evelyn, please.

37
00:02:52,040 --> 00:02:54,075
[keys jingle]

38
00:02:54,142 --> 00:02:56,744
Thank you.

39
00:02:56,811 --> 00:02:58,846
Why do you carry mace?

40
00:02:58,913 --> 00:03:01,348
Um, I live alone, so.

41
00:03:01,415 --> 00:03:03,718
But you live with me now.

42
00:03:05,787 --> 00:03:07,055
[thunder roars]

43
00:03:07,121 --> 00:03:09,389
It's getting late.
We should get you to bed soon.

44
00:03:09,456 --> 00:03:12,827
I'll just check your
blood pressure first, okay?

45
00:03:17,765 --> 00:03:19,801
Okay.

46
00:03:19,867 --> 00:03:22,870
[thunder roaring]

47
00:03:26,574 --> 00:03:29,077
I want you
to put your hand right here.

48
00:03:29,143 --> 00:03:30,310
Hm.

49
00:03:30,377 --> 00:03:31,946
Is that comfortable?

50
00:03:36,050 --> 00:03:39,352
So, is Sarah your daughter?

51
00:03:41,856 --> 00:03:45,126
You know, we never locked
our doors when we were young.

52
00:03:45,193 --> 00:03:46,127
[chuckles]

53
00:03:46,194 --> 00:03:47,394
We had no need to.

54
00:03:47,461 --> 00:03:49,197
That must've been nice.

55
00:03:49,296 --> 00:03:51,398
It was nice.

56
00:03:51,465 --> 00:03:53,901
We'd be out all day,
wandering.

57
00:03:53,968 --> 00:03:57,805
Come home in the evening
and our parents never worried.

58
00:03:57,872 --> 00:04:01,743
Maybe they did.
Maybe you just didn't notice.

59
00:04:01,809 --> 00:04:03,044
Maybe.

60
00:04:03,111 --> 00:04:05,913
[apparatus inflates]

61
00:04:05,980 --> 00:04:08,983
[apparatus deflates]

62
00:04:11,085 --> 00:04:14,387
[thunder roaring]

63
00:04:16,023 --> 00:04:17,925
Okay.

64
00:04:17,992 --> 00:04:19,060
Am I okay?

65
00:04:19,127 --> 00:04:22,230
Yeah. 116 over 75.

66
00:04:22,329 --> 00:04:23,231
You're good.

67
00:04:23,330 --> 00:04:24,699
Hmm.

68
00:04:26,501 --> 00:04:28,503
Just hold on.

69
00:04:33,207 --> 00:04:35,643
Okay.

70
00:04:35,710 --> 00:04:37,344
[beep]

71
00:04:37,410 --> 00:04:40,615
[thunder booming]

72
00:04:44,451 --> 00:04:45,352
[beeps]

73
00:04:45,418 --> 00:04:46,854
Good.

74
00:04:46,921 --> 00:04:48,355
[thunder roaring]

75
00:04:48,421 --> 00:04:50,357
There's a storm coming.

76
00:04:50,423 --> 00:04:51,659
Yeah.

77
00:04:54,762 --> 00:04:57,364
I was supposed
to fix your room.

78
00:04:57,430 --> 00:04:59,767
Oh, it's fine.
My room was made up.

79
00:04:59,834 --> 00:05:01,035
Thank you.

80
00:05:06,574 --> 00:05:08,375
Are you done?

81
00:05:08,375 --> 00:05:09,844
Yes.

82
00:05:14,148 --> 00:05:15,983
Okay. That smells nice.

83
00:05:16,050 --> 00:05:17,285
Mm-hmm.

84
00:05:17,384 --> 00:05:20,288
Did we uh,
did I show you around?

85
00:05:20,387 --> 00:05:22,489
I have everything I need.
Thank you.

86
00:05:22,557 --> 00:05:24,959
All right. Hmm.

87
00:05:26,459 --> 00:05:29,664
I forget sometimes.

88
00:05:44,579 --> 00:05:46,714
How are you feeling?

89
00:05:46,781 --> 00:05:48,481
Like hell.

90
00:05:50,518 --> 00:05:52,419
Well, I'll be right
in the next room

91
00:05:52,452 --> 00:05:54,088
if you need anything.

92
00:05:54,822 --> 00:05:57,158
Thank you. Uh...

93
00:05:57,225 --> 00:05:58,726
Julia.

94
00:05:58,793 --> 00:06:02,530
Yes, Julia,
and I'm so sorry.

95
00:06:02,597 --> 00:06:05,432
No. No apologies.
It's fine.

96
00:06:07,501 --> 00:06:09,237
Goodnight.

97
00:06:09,303 --> 00:06:11,438
Goodnight, Sarah.

98
00:06:13,908 --> 00:06:15,877
[floor creaks]

99
00:06:15,943 --> 00:06:17,011
[switch clicks]

100
00:06:18,546 --> 00:06:21,749
[keys jingle]

101
00:06:26,020 --> 00:06:29,857
[Evelyn]
Now I lay me down to sleep.

102
00:06:29,924 --> 00:06:33,861
I pray for all
the souls I keep.

103
00:06:33,928 --> 00:06:35,696
[thunder booms]

104
00:06:35,763 --> 00:06:37,665
-[loud thud]
-Shit!

105
00:06:40,067 --> 00:06:41,102
[clicks]

106
00:06:46,607 --> 00:06:48,809
[thunder booms]

107
00:06:54,282 --> 00:06:57,484
[phone rings]

108
00:07:03,591 --> 00:07:05,559
[sighs]

109
00:07:14,101 --> 00:07:15,503
[clicks switch]

110
00:07:21,709 --> 00:07:23,311
[door closes]

111
00:07:23,377 --> 00:07:26,314
[phone rings]

112
00:07:26,380 --> 00:07:29,016
Uh, shit.

113
00:07:29,083 --> 00:07:30,251
[dialing tone]

114
00:07:30,318 --> 00:07:31,886
[clears throat]

115
00:07:35,523 --> 00:07:37,124
Hi, Dad.

116
00:07:37,191 --> 00:07:38,826
[indistinct speech on phone]

117
00:07:38,893 --> 00:07:41,896
No, I'm not ignoring you.
I'm working.

118
00:07:43,531 --> 00:07:45,533
No, Dad,
I told you I probably--

119
00:07:45,599 --> 00:07:46,634
I'm not gonna make it.

120
00:07:46,701 --> 00:07:49,737
[indistinct speech on phone]

121
00:07:49,804 --> 00:07:52,039
I'm not avoiding it.

122
00:07:52,106 --> 00:07:53,641
[scoffs]

123
00:07:55,643 --> 00:07:58,746
It's just,
I-- I just got this job.

124
00:07:58,813 --> 00:08:00,948
I can't leave a few days in.

125
00:08:01,015 --> 00:08:04,552
[indistinct speech on phone]

126
00:08:06,654 --> 00:08:08,556
I don't know.

127
00:08:09,924 --> 00:08:11,859
I can't believe
you're asking this.

128
00:08:11,926 --> 00:08:15,129
[indistinct speech on phone]

129
00:08:15,629 --> 00:08:17,765
Dad, I don't know.

130
00:08:17,832 --> 00:08:19,467
[scoffs]

131
00:08:19,567 --> 00:08:21,769
Ew.
No, never mind.

132
00:08:21,836 --> 00:08:23,270
I said I don't know,
because it's not

133
00:08:23,337 --> 00:08:24,605
that kind of job.

134
00:08:24,672 --> 00:08:27,375
It could be a few days,
a few weeks.

135
00:08:27,441 --> 00:08:30,277
[dishes clatter]

136
00:08:30,344 --> 00:08:33,881
Of course, I miss her.
What kind of question is that?

137
00:08:35,850 --> 00:08:37,284
Yeah, I get it, but...

138
00:08:37,351 --> 00:08:40,388
[water runs]

139
00:08:40,454 --> 00:08:41,689
Well, what does it matter?

140
00:08:41,756 --> 00:08:44,392
No one's seen me there
in years.

141
00:08:44,458 --> 00:08:46,827
[thunder roars]

142
00:08:46,894 --> 00:08:49,997
Uh, Dad, come on.
I don't go anymore.

143
00:08:50,064 --> 00:08:51,298
You know that.

144
00:08:51,365 --> 00:08:54,503
[indistinct speech on phone]

145
00:08:54,602 --> 00:08:56,904
[door shuts and locks]

146
00:08:56,971 --> 00:08:59,106
Well, what difference
does it make?

147
00:08:59,173 --> 00:09:02,610
It doesn't change anything.
Mom knew I loved her!

148
00:09:02,610 --> 00:09:04,513
[indistinct speech on phone]

149
00:09:04,612 --> 00:09:07,248
Dad? Dad?

150
00:09:07,982 --> 00:09:11,218
Listen, I need to go,
so I'll call you again tomorrow

151
00:09:11,285 --> 00:09:13,254
and we can talk
about this then, okay?

152
00:09:13,320 --> 00:09:15,056
-[thunder booms]
-[indistinct speech on phone]

153
00:09:15,122 --> 00:09:16,323
Yes, I promise.

154
00:09:16,390 --> 00:09:18,527
[indistinct speech on phone]

155
00:09:18,626 --> 00:09:20,628
Okay.
I love you, too.

156
00:09:20,694 --> 00:09:22,696
Okay, bye.

157
00:09:23,631 --> 00:09:24,832
[clicks]

158
00:09:28,135 --> 00:09:31,205
[can pops open]

159
00:09:33,307 --> 00:09:35,109
[slurps]

160
00:09:44,852 --> 00:09:48,022
[phone rings]

161
00:09:49,023 --> 00:09:50,658
Jesus.

162
00:09:51,425 --> 00:09:56,931
Like, what is not clear about,
I'll call you to--

163
00:09:58,432 --> 00:10:01,268
[Evelyn]
What are you doing
in my house?

164
00:10:03,671 --> 00:10:05,239
Evelyn?

165
00:10:06,240 --> 00:10:08,309
How do you know my name?

166
00:10:09,076 --> 00:10:14,583
I'm your nurse.
I just helped you to bed.

167
00:10:14,648 --> 00:10:17,151
We spoke about Sarah,
your daughter.

168
00:10:18,919 --> 00:10:21,188
How about you
give me that, yeah?

169
00:10:23,858 --> 00:10:26,561
Let's put it back
by the fireplace.

170
00:10:26,627 --> 00:10:31,232
What do you think?
Yeah? Please.

171
00:10:34,935 --> 00:10:37,071
Did you paint that?

172
00:10:39,140 --> 00:10:40,474
Yes.

173
00:10:41,075 --> 00:10:45,679
Very talented.
I'm quite terrible.

174
00:10:45,746 --> 00:10:47,281
You're an artist?

175
00:10:47,348 --> 00:10:48,883
Nothing serious.

176
00:10:52,554 --> 00:10:54,355
Are those yours, too?

177
00:10:56,657 --> 00:10:58,125
Mm-hmm.

178
00:10:58,192 --> 00:11:00,194
I'd love to see
your other paintings.

179
00:11:00,261 --> 00:11:02,796
-You can hold onto that
if it makes you feel better.
-Mm-hmm.

180
00:11:02,863 --> 00:11:04,365
Is that okay?

181
00:11:07,067 --> 00:11:08,002
Okay.

182
00:11:08,068 --> 00:11:09,103
Okay.

183
00:11:10,471 --> 00:11:11,540
Go first.

184
00:11:11,606 --> 00:11:13,440
Right. Yeah, sure.

185
00:11:13,508 --> 00:11:14,875
Okay.

186
00:11:20,414 --> 00:11:21,982
Wow.

187
00:11:23,817 --> 00:11:25,953
I love the-- the detail
on this one.

188
00:11:26,020 --> 00:11:26,887
Mm.

189
00:11:26,954 --> 00:11:28,155
You have a real eye for color.

190
00:11:28,222 --> 00:11:30,157
The way they
contrast each other.

191
00:11:30,224 --> 00:11:33,093
I would've never guessed
these go together, but they do.

192
00:11:35,095 --> 00:11:38,032
My mom taught me everything.

193
00:11:38,098 --> 00:11:40,334
She had an eye like you do.

194
00:11:41,936 --> 00:11:43,804
Is this you?

195
00:11:44,639 --> 00:11:46,774
Long time ago.

196
00:11:47,642 --> 00:11:49,443
And that's your family?

197
00:11:49,511 --> 00:11:50,545
Yeah.

198
00:11:50,612 --> 00:11:52,012
Hmm.

199
00:11:53,347 --> 00:11:55,249
Anthropology.

200
00:11:55,316 --> 00:11:57,351
That's the study
of culture, right?

201
00:11:57,418 --> 00:12:00,821
Art and rituals,
and things like that?

202
00:12:02,189 --> 00:12:05,826
Oh, Randall gave me that
for our first anniversary.

203
00:12:05,893 --> 00:12:08,462
He got it at a, uh,
an art supply store

204
00:12:08,530 --> 00:12:12,866
and then he buried it
at our picnic spot.

205
00:12:12,933 --> 00:12:15,436
Is Randall the guy in the photo?

206
00:12:17,471 --> 00:12:21,408
Yeah. He-- he painted, too,

207
00:12:21,475 --> 00:12:24,512
but he took this photograph

208
00:12:24,579 --> 00:12:27,881
of me just before our wedding.

209
00:12:27,948 --> 00:12:30,084
That's the biggest smile
I've ever seen.

210
00:12:30,150 --> 00:12:31,452
Yeah.

211
00:12:32,186 --> 00:12:34,288
He must've been very special.

212
00:12:35,956 --> 00:12:38,058
We were happy.

213
00:12:39,960 --> 00:12:41,395
Hey, it's getting late.

214
00:12:41,462 --> 00:12:44,465
How about we get back,
we get you back to bed?

215
00:12:47,502 --> 00:12:49,837
I'll put this back.

216
00:12:55,876 --> 00:12:59,079
[thunder booming]

217
00:13:01,583 --> 00:13:02,517
I'm sorry.

218
00:13:02,584 --> 00:13:04,719
No, it's fine.

219
00:13:04,852 --> 00:13:06,320
Julia?

220
00:13:06,387 --> 00:13:07,522
Yeah.

221
00:13:07,589 --> 00:13:13,861
[ominous music playing]

222
00:13:19,601 --> 00:13:21,201
You okay?

223
00:13:26,641 --> 00:13:28,309
Watch your step.

224
00:13:34,415 --> 00:13:36,116
Here we are.

225
00:13:42,923 --> 00:13:45,025
There you go.

226
00:13:45,459 --> 00:13:46,761
Oh.

227
00:13:46,894 --> 00:13:48,262
[giggles]

228
00:13:48,329 --> 00:13:50,064
Thank you, Julia.

229
00:13:51,899 --> 00:13:54,168
What happened to your hands?

230
00:13:54,234 --> 00:13:55,903
Oh.

231
00:13:55,969 --> 00:13:57,672
Oh, nothing.

232
00:13:57,739 --> 00:13:59,607
Just old scars.

233
00:13:59,674 --> 00:14:00,908
Hmm.

234
00:14:01,909 --> 00:14:04,579
[exhales]

235
00:14:04,646 --> 00:14:06,980
That is one gorgeous necklace.

236
00:14:07,047 --> 00:14:10,518
Oh, why thank you.
It was my mother's.

237
00:14:10,585 --> 00:14:12,052
Is that gold?

238
00:14:12,119 --> 00:14:15,022
Um, I think so, yeah.

239
00:14:15,089 --> 00:14:17,391
What a lovely piece.

240
00:14:19,927 --> 00:14:22,129
Oh, my.

241
00:14:22,196 --> 00:14:24,298
Do you think
you could help me down?

242
00:14:24,365 --> 00:14:25,432
Of course.

243
00:14:25,499 --> 00:14:28,235
[clears throat]

244
00:14:28,302 --> 00:14:30,805
That's it. There we go.

245
00:14:30,938 --> 00:14:32,439
Oh, my.

246
00:14:35,309 --> 00:14:38,946
Ooh, you know,
all my bones creak.

247
00:14:39,012 --> 00:14:41,248
[chuckles]

248
00:14:42,517 --> 00:14:43,450
Okay.

249
00:14:43,518 --> 00:14:44,552
Ooh.

250
00:14:45,754 --> 00:14:48,188
Hmm, pray with me.

251
00:14:48,255 --> 00:14:49,490
[Julia]
Pardon?

252
00:14:50,525 --> 00:14:51,458
[taps]

253
00:14:51,526 --> 00:14:53,427
Pray with me.

254
00:14:55,563 --> 00:15:00,167
I used to think that
prayer was ridiculous, too,

255
00:15:00,234 --> 00:15:04,873
before Sarah,
but somehow asking

256
00:15:04,972 --> 00:15:09,376
an all-powerful being
for something seems arrogant.

257
00:15:09,443 --> 00:15:10,879
Hmm.

258
00:15:10,978 --> 00:15:14,883
But there is grace
in supplication.

259
00:15:14,982 --> 00:15:16,417
Hmm?

260
00:15:16,483 --> 00:15:19,987
I don't really pray
to God anymore.

261
00:15:20,855 --> 00:15:23,490
Who said anything about God?

262
00:15:23,558 --> 00:15:26,059
[thunder roars]

263
00:15:26,561 --> 00:15:30,698
Thank you, dear.
Now clasp your hands.

264
00:15:36,303 --> 00:15:41,709
Now I lay me down to sleep.

265
00:15:41,776 --> 00:15:43,310
Go on.

266
00:15:43,778 --> 00:15:45,713
Now I lay me down to sleep.

267
00:15:45,780 --> 00:15:47,147
[clears throat]

268
00:15:47,214 --> 00:15:52,587
I pray for all the souls I keep.

269
00:15:52,654 --> 00:15:57,659
If I should die
before I wake,

270
00:15:57,725 --> 00:16:02,429
I pray the souls
another body will take.

271
00:16:04,331 --> 00:16:08,770
If I should live
for a few more days,

272
00:16:08,837 --> 00:16:14,074
I pray my keeper
to guide my ways.

273
00:16:14,141 --> 00:16:16,443
In my name,

274
00:16:16,511 --> 00:16:18,078
I pray,

275
00:16:18,145 --> 00:16:20,548
I pray,

276
00:16:20,615 --> 00:16:23,050
I pray.

277
00:16:24,819 --> 00:16:29,256
Now I lay me down to sleep.

278
00:16:29,323 --> 00:16:34,261
I pray for all
of the souls I keep.

279
00:16:34,328 --> 00:16:38,198
If I should die
before I wake,

280
00:16:38,265 --> 00:16:43,605
I pray the souls
another body will take.

281
00:16:43,671 --> 00:16:47,374
If I should live
for a few more days,

282
00:16:47,441 --> 00:16:51,779
I pray my keeper
to guide my way.

283
00:16:51,846 --> 00:16:53,447
Okay.

284
00:17:16,103 --> 00:17:19,306
[thunder booms]

285
00:17:29,116 --> 00:17:33,521
Yeah.
Uh, yeah, I'll just...

286
00:17:35,122 --> 00:17:36,724
Later.

287
00:18:03,818 --> 00:18:07,321
[water runs]

288
00:18:28,977 --> 00:18:32,346
[thunder booms]

289
00:18:42,957 --> 00:18:44,092
[sniffs]

290
00:18:44,191 --> 00:18:45,459
Not bad.

291
00:18:51,666 --> 00:18:53,266
That's cute.

292
00:18:55,069 --> 00:18:56,004
[sniffs]

293
00:18:56,070 --> 00:18:57,572
That's gross.

294
00:18:58,840 --> 00:19:01,809
[thunder booms]

295
00:19:05,079 --> 00:19:08,049
Color contrast, my ass.

296
00:19:08,116 --> 00:19:09,617
You're one dark lady.

297
00:19:09,684 --> 00:19:11,919
[Evelyn coughs]

298
00:19:13,888 --> 00:19:15,890
Yeah, you're okay.

299
00:19:22,329 --> 00:19:25,265
[floor creaks]

300
00:19:25,332 --> 00:19:31,539
[sinister music playing]

301
00:19:50,257 --> 00:19:52,259
Weird.

302
00:20:00,267 --> 00:20:03,538
[thunder booms]

303
00:20:05,740 --> 00:20:06,908
[thud upstairs]

304
00:20:12,245 --> 00:20:17,919
[winds howling]

305
00:20:30,263 --> 00:20:36,470
[sinister music playing]

306
00:20:44,311 --> 00:20:45,947
[gulps]

307
00:20:46,013 --> 00:20:52,019
[sinister music playing]

308
00:21:00,027 --> 00:21:01,394
[slurps]

309
00:21:01,461 --> 00:21:07,602
[music continues to play]

310
00:21:16,409 --> 00:21:20,681
[house creaking]

311
00:21:39,033 --> 00:21:42,036
[clock ticking]

312
00:21:50,545 --> 00:21:52,947
[Julia clears throat]

313
00:21:56,150 --> 00:21:59,386
[thunder roaring]

314
00:22:06,861 --> 00:22:09,797
[sighs]

315
00:22:15,870 --> 00:22:18,873
[clock ticking]

316
00:22:39,227 --> 00:22:41,896
[creaking sounds]

317
00:22:47,034 --> 00:22:50,504
-[loud thunder]
-[thudding sounds]

318
00:22:52,607 --> 00:22:54,809
[creaking continues]

319
00:22:59,814 --> 00:23:00,848
[thudding]

320
00:23:04,919 --> 00:23:07,021
[loud thunder]

321
00:23:10,457 --> 00:23:12,459
[floor creaks above]

322
00:23:12,459 --> 00:23:18,666
[sinister music playing]

323
00:23:27,742 --> 00:23:32,479
Evelyn? Are you up again?

324
00:23:32,513 --> 00:23:33,981
[knocking sound]

325
00:23:37,551 --> 00:23:39,687
[knocking continues]

326
00:23:39,754 --> 00:23:45,960
[sinister music playing]

327
00:24:00,374 --> 00:24:01,575
Can I help you?

328
00:24:01,642 --> 00:24:03,044
Is Evelyn home?

329
00:24:03,110 --> 00:24:04,345
Sorry, who are you?

330
00:24:04,412 --> 00:24:07,415
Randall.
You're Julia, right?

331
00:24:07,515 --> 00:24:09,850
Your agency put us in touch.

332
00:24:09,917 --> 00:24:12,153
Yeah, yeah.
Of course, hi.

333
00:24:12,219 --> 00:24:13,421
Come in.

334
00:24:18,059 --> 00:24:18,993
[door shuts]

335
00:24:19,060 --> 00:24:19,927
You're Evelyn's husband.

336
00:24:19,994 --> 00:24:23,331
Well, not for a long time now.

337
00:24:23,397 --> 00:24:24,832
Oh.

338
00:24:24,899 --> 00:24:26,233
Is she up?

339
00:24:26,300 --> 00:24:27,768
I just put her to bed.

340
00:24:27,835 --> 00:24:31,238
I hope she's awake.
I drove a long way out.

341
00:24:31,305 --> 00:24:34,342
She should be.
She was just praying, so...

342
00:24:34,408 --> 00:24:36,110
Evie, praying?

343
00:24:37,345 --> 00:24:38,813
Yeah.

344
00:24:49,557 --> 00:24:51,192
[Julia clears throat]

345
00:24:51,258 --> 00:24:53,861
Did you-- did you hit the storm
on the way here?

346
00:24:53,928 --> 00:24:56,364
No, I came
from the other direction.

347
00:24:56,998 --> 00:24:59,667
I hope it doesn't get too bad.

348
00:24:59,734 --> 00:25:02,570
How is she doing?

349
00:25:02,603 --> 00:25:04,839
Uh, it's been
a pretty rough night.

350
00:25:04,905 --> 00:25:07,875
She's been kind of in and out.

351
00:25:09,677 --> 00:25:11,779
She spoke about you, though.

352
00:25:16,117 --> 00:25:17,818
Is something wrong?

353
00:25:19,086 --> 00:25:20,321
No.

354
00:25:21,222 --> 00:25:26,160
Uh, no. It's just,
I haven't seen this one
in a long time.

355
00:25:28,696 --> 00:25:31,599
[footsteps]

356
00:25:31,632 --> 00:25:37,838
[sinister music playing]

357
00:25:57,625 --> 00:26:00,494
[floor creaks]

358
00:26:00,628 --> 00:26:06,767
[music continues to play]

359
00:26:26,353 --> 00:26:28,656
There she is.

360
00:26:28,656 --> 00:26:30,224
Randall?

361
00:26:30,291 --> 00:26:31,292
Hey, Evie.

362
00:26:31,358 --> 00:26:32,760
Huh.

363
00:26:35,162 --> 00:26:36,664
You got old.

364
00:26:36,664 --> 00:26:38,899
Yeah, they say that happens.

365
00:26:39,967 --> 00:26:42,369
You're still as lovely as ever.

366
00:26:43,070 --> 00:26:45,106
And you're still full of shit.

367
00:26:45,172 --> 00:26:46,707
[chuckles]

368
00:26:46,774 --> 00:26:48,042
I've missed you.

369
00:26:48,109 --> 00:26:49,310
I know.

370
00:26:52,379 --> 00:26:54,448
Is Earl here with you?

371
00:26:54,516 --> 00:26:59,186
My brother died 12 years ago.
You went to the funeral.

372
00:27:00,754 --> 00:27:02,156
I did?

373
00:27:02,223 --> 00:27:03,924
It's okay.

374
00:27:03,991 --> 00:27:06,694
None of us are
what we used to be, right?

375
00:27:09,730 --> 00:27:11,699
And Marlene?

376
00:27:11,699 --> 00:27:12,967
She left me.

377
00:27:13,033 --> 00:27:15,236
That's been
a long time now, too.

378
00:27:16,237 --> 00:27:17,171
I'm sorry.

379
00:27:17,238 --> 00:27:18,172
[chuckles]

380
00:27:18,239 --> 00:27:20,141
No, you're not.

381
00:27:20,207 --> 00:27:21,375
No, I'm not.

382
00:27:21,442 --> 00:27:23,210
[chuckles]

383
00:27:24,546 --> 00:27:26,280
How long are you staying?

384
00:27:26,347 --> 00:27:27,748
As long as I need to.

385
00:27:28,916 --> 00:27:31,218
You have help now,

386
00:27:31,285 --> 00:27:34,255
so you don't need to worry
about anything.

387
00:27:35,923 --> 00:27:38,325
You have been thinking
about her.

388
00:27:38,859 --> 00:27:40,728
Every day.

389
00:27:41,729 --> 00:27:43,330
Me too.

390
00:27:48,335 --> 00:27:50,771
So why are you here?

391
00:27:55,376 --> 00:27:57,745
[paper shuffles]

392
00:27:57,778 --> 00:28:00,381
Where did you find
this inscription?

393
00:28:01,916 --> 00:28:04,418
Why didn't you wait
for me to get back?

394
00:28:04,485 --> 00:28:08,956
We could've discussed it,
figured out something together.

395
00:28:10,357 --> 00:28:14,495
Where is it, Evelyn?
I know you have it.

396
00:28:14,563 --> 00:28:15,796
No.

397
00:28:15,863 --> 00:28:17,097
Nobody else knows
where we buried it.

398
00:28:17,164 --> 00:28:19,534
No. No.

399
00:28:19,601 --> 00:28:21,769
-Why would you take it?
-No.

400
00:28:21,835 --> 00:28:25,674
If it's for this,
you know what can happen.

401
00:28:26,273 --> 00:28:28,209
-Where is it?
-[Julia] Hey.

402
00:28:28,275 --> 00:28:29,076
Go away.

403
00:28:29,143 --> 00:28:30,244
I'm trying to protect you!

404
00:28:30,311 --> 00:28:32,846
-No.
-Hey! Don't touch her.

405
00:28:32,913 --> 00:28:36,217
Leave me, leave me,
leave me alone.

406
00:28:36,283 --> 00:28:37,851
[Evelyn crying]

407
00:28:37,918 --> 00:28:39,554
[Evelyn]
Go away.

408
00:28:39,621 --> 00:28:42,524
You need to leave.
Now.

409
00:28:42,591 --> 00:28:45,793
[Evelyn sobs]

410
00:28:48,095 --> 00:28:49,664
[Evelyn]
Make him go. Make him go.

411
00:28:49,797 --> 00:28:50,864
Okay.

412
00:28:50,931 --> 00:28:51,932
[Evelyn]
Make sure he leaves.

413
00:28:51,999 --> 00:28:53,367
[Julia]
I promise.

414
00:28:54,034 --> 00:28:56,036
[Evelyn]
I don't wanna see him.

415
00:28:56,103 --> 00:28:58,339
If you don't get out
of this house in 30 seconds,

416
00:28:58,405 --> 00:29:01,308
I'm calling the police.
I don't care who you are.

417
00:29:04,345 --> 00:29:07,348
You have no idea
what's going on here.

418
00:29:07,414 --> 00:29:10,417
[Evelyn groans]

419
00:29:13,087 --> 00:29:14,154
[Julia]
Yeah.

420
00:29:14,221 --> 00:29:15,489
It's gonna be okay, all right?

421
00:29:15,557 --> 00:29:18,492
[Evelyn]
Please, please get rid of him.

422
00:29:18,560 --> 00:29:20,294
I never wanna see him again.

423
00:29:20,361 --> 00:29:22,564
[Julia]
All right, just--
just calm down.

424
00:29:22,631 --> 00:29:24,164
I'll be right back.

425
00:29:28,035 --> 00:29:30,070
Where are you hiding it?

426
00:29:30,137 --> 00:29:32,873
[Julia]
Hey! Get out!

427
00:29:32,940 --> 00:29:39,146
[sinister music playing]

428
00:29:53,394 --> 00:29:55,296
Just leave!

429
00:29:57,064 --> 00:29:59,867
Watch yourself.

430
00:30:07,174 --> 00:30:08,710
[locking]

431
00:30:08,777 --> 00:30:14,982
[sinister music playing]

432
00:30:22,590 --> 00:30:25,092
[car starts]

433
00:30:26,994 --> 00:30:30,197
[car drives away]

434
00:30:31,666 --> 00:30:33,867
[thunder roars]

435
00:30:33,934 --> 00:30:37,838
[wind whooshes]

436
00:30:45,412 --> 00:30:48,916
Evelyn, what are you doing?
It's freezing.

437
00:30:51,018 --> 00:30:53,588
[Evelyn] I wanna be out here
when I pass.

438
00:30:54,556 --> 00:30:57,324
[Julia] Let's not talk about
that. You've still got time.

439
00:30:59,259 --> 00:31:02,229
[Evelyn] Why would anyone
want a job like this?

440
00:31:03,230 --> 00:31:06,367
Why would you want to
watch someone die?

441
00:31:07,669 --> 00:31:10,270
[Julia] Because no one
should have to die alone.

442
00:31:11,840 --> 00:31:14,041
[Evelyn] We all die alone.

443
00:31:14,942 --> 00:31:16,678
[Julia] What was that all
about up there?

444
00:31:17,545 --> 00:31:21,783
[Evelyn] Oh,
we don't agree on things.
We never did, really.

445
00:31:22,751 --> 00:31:26,954
I tried to get him
to understand
but he-- he blames me.

446
00:31:28,389 --> 00:31:30,257
[Julia] What happened to Sarah?

447
00:31:32,159 --> 00:31:36,263
[Evelyn] Oh, Sarah.
I miss her so much.

448
00:31:39,099 --> 00:31:40,702
Can't hide from our past.

449
00:31:40,769 --> 00:31:44,506
Sometimes we have
to confront it and accept it.

450
00:31:46,708 --> 00:31:47,809
[Julia] Is everything okay?

451
00:31:47,876 --> 00:31:49,977
[Evelyn] I'm going to be sick.

452
00:31:49,977 --> 00:31:52,547
[Julia] Come on,
let's go inside.

453
00:31:52,614 --> 00:31:55,617
[Evelyn groans]

454
00:31:57,117 --> 00:31:58,051
[throws up]

455
00:31:58,118 --> 00:32:00,622
Oh, dear. Come here.

456
00:32:00,688 --> 00:32:03,725
[groans]

457
00:32:03,792 --> 00:32:05,727
Ugh, oh, I'm so sorry.

458
00:32:05,794 --> 00:32:07,829
No, it's okay. It's fine.

459
00:32:07,896 --> 00:32:11,165
Let's get you cleaned up, okay?
I'll find you a blanket.

460
00:32:11,231 --> 00:32:17,438
[sinister music playing]

461
00:32:26,146 --> 00:32:27,381
All right.

462
00:32:33,755 --> 00:32:35,723
Evelyn?

463
00:32:36,925 --> 00:32:40,127
[clattering noises in distance]

464
00:32:43,531 --> 00:32:46,200
Oh, my... Evelyn?

465
00:32:46,266 --> 00:32:47,669
[Evelyn snarls]

466
00:32:47,735 --> 00:32:49,604
Evelyn, what are you doing?

467
00:32:49,671 --> 00:32:51,205
[snarling]

468
00:32:51,271 --> 00:32:52,507
Stop that, please.

469
00:32:52,574 --> 00:32:55,577
[growls, snarls]

470
00:32:56,945 --> 00:33:00,147
[pants]

471
00:33:01,148 --> 00:33:02,349
Evelyn!

472
00:33:02,416 --> 00:33:05,553
[footsteps thud away]

473
00:33:06,554 --> 00:33:07,889
[Evelyn laughs]

474
00:33:07,956 --> 00:33:09,557
[Julia]
Stop.

475
00:33:14,061 --> 00:33:15,897
[loud thuds]

476
00:33:15,964 --> 00:33:17,297
Eve--

477
00:33:20,902 --> 00:33:24,104
[record playing in background]

478
00:33:26,608 --> 00:33:28,743
Jesus Christ.

479
00:33:29,376 --> 00:33:31,245
[Sarah on recorder]
<i>It's not working.</i>

480
00:33:31,311 --> 00:33:34,649
[Evelyn on recorder]
<i>The song will work.</i>
<i>It always works.</i>

481
00:33:34,716 --> 00:33:35,917
[Sarah on recorder]
<i>Brush my hair.</i>

482
00:33:35,984 --> 00:33:37,284
<i>What the fuck is this?</i>

483
00:33:37,351 --> 00:33:39,119
[Evelyn on recorder]
<i>Sure, my love.</i>

484
00:33:40,922 --> 00:33:44,091
[Sarah on recorder]
<i>It don't feel so good.</i>
<i>My tummy hurts.</i>

485
00:33:45,092 --> 00:33:47,327
[Evelyn on recorder]
<i>Do you want me</i>
<i>to rub your tummy?</i>

486
00:33:49,329 --> 00:33:50,598
[Sarah on recorder]
<i>Mom?</i>

487
00:33:50,665 --> 00:33:52,332
[Evelyn on recorder]
<i>What is it?</i>

488
00:33:52,399 --> 00:33:54,368
[Sarah on recorder]
<i>Why do you have that?</i>

489
00:33:54,434 --> 00:33:56,236
[Evelyn on recorder]
<i>Oh, this?</i>

490
00:33:56,303 --> 00:33:58,540
[Sarah on recorder]
<i>Are you taping me?</i>

491
00:33:58,606 --> 00:34:01,275
-[Evelyn on recorder] <i>I...</i>
-[Julia] Where the fuck am I?

492
00:34:01,341 --> 00:34:03,778
[Evelyn on recorder]
<i>I was-- I was worried about you</i>
<i>and wanted to record</i>

493
00:34:03,845 --> 00:34:05,145
<i>any changes.</i>

494
00:34:05,212 --> 00:34:07,281
[Sarah on recorder]
<i>Changes?</i>

495
00:34:07,347 --> 00:34:10,484
[Evelyn on recorder]
<i>Sorry, I should've asked you.</i>
<i>I'll turn it off.</i>

496
00:34:12,119 --> 00:34:13,555
[Sarah on recorder]
<i>Is it off?</i>

497
00:34:13,621 --> 00:34:15,222
[Evelyn on recorder]
<i>Yes.</i>

498
00:34:16,758 --> 00:34:18,292
[Sarah on recorder]
<i>Don't ever do that again!</i>

499
00:34:18,358 --> 00:34:19,994
-[tape clatters]
-shit.

500
00:34:20,127 --> 00:34:21,261
[Evelyn on recorder]
<i>Sarah?</i>

501
00:34:21,328 --> 00:34:23,163
[Sarah on recorder]
<i>Get out!</i>

502
00:34:25,332 --> 00:34:27,134
[Evelyn on recorder]
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

503
00:34:28,036 --> 00:34:28,970
[clicks recorder off]

504
00:34:29,037 --> 00:34:35,242
[sinister music playing]

505
00:34:44,184 --> 00:34:45,720
[Julia]
Okay.

506
00:34:47,154 --> 00:34:52,292
[sinister music playing]

507
00:34:54,261 --> 00:34:56,798
Oh, my God, Evelyn,
what did you do?

508
00:34:56,864 --> 00:35:02,870
[ominous music playing]

509
00:35:14,181 --> 00:35:15,917
What the hell?

510
00:35:15,984 --> 00:35:21,188
[sinister music playing]

511
00:35:30,798 --> 00:35:32,232
What is this?

512
00:35:32,299 --> 00:35:38,506
[music continues to play]

513
00:36:02,396 --> 00:36:08,536
[ominous music playing]

514
00:36:15,043 --> 00:36:17,444
[Julia clears throat]

515
00:36:18,245 --> 00:36:21,549
[footsteps shuffling]

516
00:36:27,755 --> 00:36:30,758
[floor creaks]

517
00:36:36,664 --> 00:36:38,265
Hello?

518
00:36:39,801 --> 00:36:43,504
[floor creaks]

519
00:36:51,478 --> 00:36:54,682
[door creaks]

520
00:37:02,456 --> 00:37:05,292
What... What is...

521
00:37:05,292 --> 00:37:07,327
[soft gasps]

522
00:37:14,001 --> 00:37:15,837
What the fuck?

523
00:37:15,903 --> 00:37:21,909
[sinister music playing]

524
00:37:26,114 --> 00:37:27,682
[loud thud]

525
00:37:27,749 --> 00:37:30,317
[Peter]
Is there a back door?

526
00:37:30,317 --> 00:37:32,419
[Randall]
I think I can open it.

527
00:37:33,320 --> 00:37:35,223
Pete!

528
00:37:35,322 --> 00:37:36,791
Go check upstairs.

529
00:37:36,858 --> 00:37:38,726
Sh-- shit.

530
00:37:39,927 --> 00:37:40,862
Oh!

531
00:37:40,928 --> 00:37:44,031
[footsteps approach]

532
00:37:51,338 --> 00:37:53,007
[clicks switch]

533
00:37:53,074 --> 00:37:59,346
[sinister music playing]

534
00:38:05,953 --> 00:38:06,988
[clicks switch]

535
00:38:11,058 --> 00:38:13,060
[Peter]
Office is clear.

536
00:38:16,197 --> 00:38:18,365
[Randall]
Kitchen's clear.

537
00:38:19,967 --> 00:38:22,904
Evelyn, where are you?
I just want to talk!

538
00:38:22,970 --> 00:38:28,441
[sinister music playing]

539
00:38:35,016 --> 00:38:37,885
[door creaks open]

540
00:38:42,389 --> 00:38:43,891
Okay.

541
00:38:47,195 --> 00:38:49,931
[thunder booms]

542
00:38:52,867 --> 00:38:56,003
[floor creaking]

543
00:39:35,843 --> 00:39:36,777
Hey.

544
00:39:36,844 --> 00:39:37,578
[screams]

545
00:39:37,645 --> 00:39:40,781
Oh, fuck! Oh!

546
00:39:40,848 --> 00:39:42,984
[Edgar coughing]

547
00:39:43,050 --> 00:39:44,819
[panting]

548
00:39:44,886 --> 00:39:45,987
Calm down.

549
00:39:46,053 --> 00:39:48,556
Where do I go?
Where the fuck do I go?

550
00:39:50,258 --> 00:39:51,692
Shit!

551
00:39:55,963 --> 00:39:58,532
Okay, okay.

552
00:39:58,599 --> 00:40:00,034
Just find something.

553
00:40:00,101 --> 00:40:01,602
There's gotta be something
in here.

554
00:40:01,669 --> 00:40:04,972
Okay. Find scissors.

555
00:40:06,173 --> 00:40:07,208
Okay.

556
00:40:07,275 --> 00:40:09,577
Shit.
Fucking...

557
00:40:11,279 --> 00:40:13,581
Fucking shit!

558
00:40:15,016 --> 00:40:16,350
[Edgar]
She blinded me, man.

559
00:40:16,416 --> 00:40:17,718
[Peter]
Yeah, well.

560
00:40:17,785 --> 00:40:18,819
-[Edgar] I'm scared.
-[Randall] Quiet!

561
00:40:18,886 --> 00:40:20,420
[Edgar]
It fucking burns!

562
00:40:20,487 --> 00:40:22,489
[Randall] Hey, man up!
You grab him.

563
00:40:22,556 --> 00:40:24,025
I can't look
for anyone right now.

564
00:40:24,091 --> 00:40:25,026
Hey, shut up. All right?

565
00:40:25,092 --> 00:40:27,228
Just be quiet.

566
00:40:27,295 --> 00:40:28,729
We just want to talk.

567
00:40:28,796 --> 00:40:30,430
We're running out of time.

568
00:40:30,497 --> 00:40:32,934
Give me a minute.
Go downstairs.

569
00:40:34,501 --> 00:40:37,371
I'm not gonna hurt anybody.
Can we talk?

570
00:40:37,437 --> 00:40:38,572
I'd like to explain.

571
00:40:38,639 --> 00:40:39,941
Stay away!

572
00:40:40,007 --> 00:40:41,742
This is not how
I wanted this to go.

573
00:40:41,809 --> 00:40:44,178
How did you
want this to go?

574
00:40:44,245 --> 00:40:45,746
This is a misunderstanding.

575
00:40:45,813 --> 00:40:48,149
Just leave us alone!

576
00:40:48,816 --> 00:40:50,952
You can stay in there
if it makes you feel better.

577
00:40:51,018 --> 00:40:52,653
It does.

578
00:40:52,720 --> 00:40:54,422
Evelyn's in trouble.
Where is she?

579
00:40:54,487 --> 00:40:55,756
I don't know!

580
00:40:55,823 --> 00:40:57,758
And I wouldn't tell you
if I did.

581
00:40:57,825 --> 00:40:59,293
Is she still in the house?

582
00:40:59,360 --> 00:41:01,662
What the fuck did I just say?

583
00:41:01,729 --> 00:41:05,266
Nothing I can tell you will
make you believe me.

584
00:41:05,333 --> 00:41:08,536
Hell, I didn't believe it myself
and I lived through it.

585
00:41:08,536 --> 00:41:09,971
Through what?

586
00:41:10,037 --> 00:41:11,172
[sighs]

587
00:41:11,238 --> 00:41:12,940
We had a child.

588
00:41:14,842 --> 00:41:17,545
She died because
we couldn't protect her.

589
00:41:19,013 --> 00:41:20,247
That's a lie.

590
00:41:20,314 --> 00:41:23,451
We could've protected her,
but we got careless.

591
00:41:24,251 --> 00:41:27,822
We thought we knew better
and it destroyed us.

592
00:41:27,888 --> 00:41:30,925
Evelyn never forgave herself
and...

593
00:41:30,992 --> 00:41:32,860
And what?

594
00:41:33,661 --> 00:41:35,629
She was my first love,
you know?

595
00:41:35,696 --> 00:41:37,398
[Peter]
Randall, we got her!

596
00:41:37,465 --> 00:41:39,000
Just leave her alone!

597
00:41:39,066 --> 00:41:42,203
I'm sorry.
This is for your own good.

598
00:41:42,269 --> 00:41:44,638
[door locks shut]

599
00:41:44,705 --> 00:41:46,140
Let me out!

600
00:41:49,276 --> 00:41:52,279
[lock rattling]

601
00:41:56,183 --> 00:42:00,287
[Edgar]
Randall, Peter, we got her.

602
00:42:02,123 --> 00:42:03,190
Calm down.

603
00:42:03,257 --> 00:42:05,659
[Evelyn]
Get out of my house!

604
00:42:05,726 --> 00:42:07,728
[Randall]
Take a deep breath.
Calm down.

605
00:42:07,795 --> 00:42:08,829
[Evelyn]
Don't touch me.

606
00:42:08,896 --> 00:42:10,731
Everything is gonna be okay.

607
00:42:10,798 --> 00:42:13,734
[Evelyn]
Of course, it's you.
Stay away.

608
00:42:13,801 --> 00:42:17,204
Peter, give her some space.

609
00:42:19,607 --> 00:42:24,111
Evelyn, put that down.
You shouldn't be touching that.

610
00:42:25,613 --> 00:42:29,150
Please, hand it over, Evie.

611
00:42:31,419 --> 00:42:32,753
Let me take it off your hands.

612
00:42:32,820 --> 00:42:34,889
I just want to put it
someplace safe.

613
00:42:34,955 --> 00:42:38,092
[Evelyn]
There is no place safe.

614
00:42:38,159 --> 00:42:40,394
It was safe until you started
messing with it.

615
00:42:40,461 --> 00:42:41,629
Why, Evie?

616
00:42:41,662 --> 00:42:44,765
[Evelyn]
Because I miss her!

617
00:42:44,832 --> 00:42:46,634
I'm sorry about
the way things turned out.

618
00:42:46,667 --> 00:42:48,969
Yeah, you left me
right after she died

619
00:42:49,036 --> 00:42:51,238
when I needed you the most.

620
00:42:51,305 --> 00:42:52,339
[sobs]

621
00:42:52,406 --> 00:42:54,475
What do you want me to say?

622
00:42:54,543 --> 00:42:56,644
That I couldn't face you after?

623
00:42:56,644 --> 00:42:59,680
That the-- the guilt
ate me up inside?

624
00:42:59,747 --> 00:43:02,950
I got it wrong and I've had
to live with that.

625
00:43:04,553 --> 00:43:05,820
But I can do it right this time.

626
00:43:05,886 --> 00:43:08,189
I know how. Trust me.

627
00:43:08,255 --> 00:43:09,890
Trust you?

628
00:43:09,957 --> 00:43:12,193
That's what got her killed.

629
00:43:12,960 --> 00:43:16,230
I translated one of the words
that you sent me.

630
00:43:16,297 --> 00:43:17,498
[paper shuffles]

631
00:43:17,566 --> 00:43:20,101
It's an incantation, isn't it?

632
00:43:20,167 --> 00:43:21,702
Tell me!

633
00:43:21,769 --> 00:43:23,671
We can still do the right thing.

634
00:43:24,472 --> 00:43:28,109
That's your weakness, always
wanting to do the right thing,

635
00:43:28,175 --> 00:43:32,913
huh, when there's only pain
and loss and suffering.

636
00:43:32,980 --> 00:43:36,117
This is not going
to bring Sarah back!

637
00:43:37,284 --> 00:43:38,686
Give it to me!

638
00:43:39,253 --> 00:43:44,892
Why? [voice deepening]
So you can bury me again?

639
00:43:44,959 --> 00:43:47,928
[Randall]
Who-- who am I talking
to right now?

640
00:43:47,995 --> 00:43:50,698
What have you done with Evelyn?

641
00:43:50,764 --> 00:43:53,602
I wear her like a coat.

642
00:43:53,701 --> 00:43:55,302
[growls]

643
00:43:55,369 --> 00:43:57,004
[coughs]

644
00:43:59,773 --> 00:44:00,708
[body thuds]

645
00:44:00,774 --> 00:44:03,978
[yells, groans]

646
00:44:08,583 --> 00:44:09,750
Oh, my God.

647
00:44:09,817 --> 00:44:10,818
[Edgar]
Let's get outta here.

648
00:44:10,885 --> 00:44:12,820
Oh, let's call the others.

649
00:44:12,887 --> 00:44:15,089
Get out, quick, quick.

650
00:44:17,191 --> 00:44:20,194
[fire crackling]

651
00:44:27,536 --> 00:44:30,738
[Evelyn low giggling]

652
00:44:38,746 --> 00:44:41,650
[dragging sounds]

653
00:44:41,749 --> 00:44:47,922
[sinister music playing]

654
00:45:08,242 --> 00:45:10,978
[groans]

655
00:45:11,045 --> 00:45:17,251
[music continues to play]

656
00:45:23,257 --> 00:45:26,528
[wind whooshes]

657
00:45:26,595 --> 00:45:29,797
[clock ticking]

658
00:45:36,804 --> 00:45:38,906
[exhales]

659
00:45:42,876 --> 00:45:45,813
[ringing sound]

660
00:45:45,879 --> 00:45:52,086
[sinister music playing]

661
00:45:59,460 --> 00:46:02,664
[takes deep breath]

662
00:46:03,197 --> 00:46:06,267
[clattering sounds]

663
00:46:08,637 --> 00:46:12,540
[Julia]
Evelyn? Evelyn?

664
00:46:12,607 --> 00:46:15,342
[footsteps]

665
00:46:16,910 --> 00:46:19,413
Oh, my God,
what did they do to you?

666
00:46:20,414 --> 00:46:21,849
They're gone now.

667
00:46:22,550 --> 00:46:26,153
Let's get you changed.
Oh, my goodness.

668
00:46:26,220 --> 00:46:29,957
Here we go.
Where are you hurt?

669
00:46:31,526 --> 00:46:34,395
Oh, look at your hand.
What did they do to you?

670
00:46:34,461 --> 00:46:38,866
Okay, let's-- let's sit here.
Yeah, there you go.

671
00:46:40,868 --> 00:46:42,069
-Want to give me that?
-No.

672
00:46:42,136 --> 00:46:43,971
Wash your hands, okay?

673
00:46:44,038 --> 00:46:45,973
Okay. Okay. Here we go.

674
00:46:46,040 --> 00:46:47,875
[water running]

675
00:46:47,875 --> 00:46:52,112
All right. There you go.

676
00:46:53,280 --> 00:46:55,482
Got this one.
That's great.

677
00:46:58,886 --> 00:47:00,588
Where's your phone?

678
00:47:00,655 --> 00:47:02,956
-In the office.
-Okay.

679
00:47:04,091 --> 00:47:08,195
We'll find it, yeah?
You'll be okay.

680
00:47:08,262 --> 00:47:09,897
Yeah.

681
00:47:11,800 --> 00:47:13,467
Here we are. All right.

682
00:47:14,769 --> 00:47:16,904
Okay, you good?

683
00:47:16,937 --> 00:47:20,974
-Yeah, I'm fine.
-All right. Here we are.

684
00:47:25,814 --> 00:47:29,684
All right.
Let's sit right here.

685
00:47:29,751 --> 00:47:31,485
Where is it?

686
00:47:32,620 --> 00:47:35,657
Okay, great.

687
00:47:35,724 --> 00:47:37,559
For fuck's sake!

688
00:47:37,625 --> 00:47:38,926
[slams phone]

689
00:47:38,992 --> 00:47:40,994
What do they want?

690
00:47:42,463 --> 00:47:45,032
What-- this?
What-- what is it?

691
00:47:45,099 --> 00:47:47,334
Is it worth a lot of money?

692
00:47:49,002 --> 00:47:50,938
[groans loudly]

693
00:47:51,606 --> 00:47:52,640
[thunder rumbling]

694
00:47:52,707 --> 00:47:54,241
This is not--

695
00:47:56,443 --> 00:47:58,946
You should be surrounded
by loved ones,

696
00:47:59,012 --> 00:48:01,115
not by someone like me.

697
00:48:04,084 --> 00:48:07,121
[Evelyn on recorder]
<i>Sarah, if you ever get</i>
<i>to hear this,</i>

698
00:48:07,187 --> 00:48:10,692
<i>your suffering is</i>
<i>because of us.</i>

699
00:48:10,759 --> 00:48:13,460
<i>Too many risks.</i>

700
00:48:13,528 --> 00:48:16,163
<i>Too much contact</i>
<i>with the other side.</i>

701
00:48:16,230 --> 00:48:18,132
[Randall on recorder]
<i>We have to bury her.</i>

702
00:48:18,198 --> 00:48:20,968
[Evelyn on recorder]
<i>I'm sorry we put</i>
<i>all this ahead of you.</i>

703
00:48:21,034 --> 00:48:23,638
<i>I'll never expose you</i>
<i>to this again.</i>

704
00:48:24,672 --> 00:48:26,140
<i>What's wrong with us?</i>

705
00:48:26,206 --> 00:48:28,976
[Randall on recorder]
<i>Okay. Father, start the prayer.</i>

706
00:48:29,042 --> 00:48:30,812
[father on recorder
speaking Latin]

707
00:48:30,879 --> 00:48:32,980
[Evelyn on recorder]
<i>I'm sorry.</i>
<i>It was meant for--</i>

708
00:48:33,046 --> 00:48:34,582
[Sarah on recorder]
<i>Stop, stop.</i>
<i>Please don't do this.</i>

709
00:48:34,649 --> 00:48:36,851
[Evelyn on recorder]
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

710
00:48:36,984 --> 00:48:38,185
Is that...

711
00:48:38,252 --> 00:48:39,554
[Sarah on recorder]
<i>Help me. Mommy!</i>

712
00:48:39,621 --> 00:48:41,155
-...your baby?
<i>-No, mommy, please.</i>

713
00:48:41,221 --> 00:48:42,624
[Evelyn on recorder]
<i>She's not okay.</i>

714
00:48:42,690 --> 00:48:44,158
[Randall on recorder]
<i>She will be fine.</i>

715
00:48:44,224 --> 00:48:45,560
[Sarah on recorder]
<i>Stop! Stop!</i>

716
00:48:45,627 --> 00:48:47,227
[Father on recorder]
<i>She'll look in the box.</i>

717
00:48:47,294 --> 00:48:48,228
[Evelyn on recorder]
<i>What-- what is this?</i>

718
00:48:48,295 --> 00:48:50,063
[indiscernible speech]

719
00:48:51,465 --> 00:48:52,834
[Evelyn on recorder]
<i>Look at her!</i>

720
00:48:52,901 --> 00:48:54,201
[Sarah on recorder]
<i>Help!</i>

721
00:48:54,268 --> 00:48:55,737
[father on recorder
speaking Latin]

722
00:48:55,804 --> 00:48:57,438
[Sarah on recorder]
<i>Stop! Stop! Stop!</i>

723
00:48:57,505 --> 00:48:59,106
[Randall on recorder]
<i>There he is.</i>

724
00:48:59,173 --> 00:49:00,708
[Sarah on recorder]
<i>Get off!</i>

725
00:49:00,775 --> 00:49:02,777
[Randall on recorder]
<i>We've got to bury the de--</i>

726
00:49:03,243 --> 00:49:05,245
Let's get you warmed up.

727
00:49:05,312 --> 00:49:08,315
[humming]

728
00:49:13,888 --> 00:49:16,658
I brought her to evil.

729
00:49:16,724 --> 00:49:19,092
It's my fault.

730
00:49:19,159 --> 00:49:21,696
-It's all my fault.
-Don't say that.

731
00:49:24,498 --> 00:49:26,033
It's true.

732
00:49:26,099 --> 00:49:29,637
All right. You're okay.

733
00:49:29,704 --> 00:49:31,038
Okay.

734
00:49:31,104 --> 00:49:33,575
No, no. I don't want it.

735
00:49:33,641 --> 00:49:35,209
Okay.

736
00:49:35,743 --> 00:49:38,746
[pants]

737
00:49:42,216 --> 00:49:45,720
Nice, nice, nice, nice, nice.
You feeling better?

738
00:49:48,222 --> 00:49:49,189
This one's nice.

739
00:49:49,256 --> 00:49:52,459
[thunder rumbles]

740
00:49:55,930 --> 00:49:57,464
Things happen, Evelyn.

741
00:49:57,532 --> 00:50:00,234
I'm sure you and Randall
were great parents.

742
00:50:01,936 --> 00:50:04,137
You don't know that.

743
00:50:06,139 --> 00:50:09,142
I know I blamed myself
for my mom's death.

744
00:50:10,745 --> 00:50:15,382
I mean, I know,
I didn't make her sick,

745
00:50:15,449 --> 00:50:19,787
but I-- I should've been there
for her, and I-- I just-- I--

746
00:50:19,854 --> 00:50:21,355
I couldn't do it.

747
00:50:23,190 --> 00:50:25,994
It's easier to take care
of strangers.

748
00:50:26,059 --> 00:50:27,127
Hmm.

749
00:50:27,194 --> 00:50:29,597
[knocking on door]

750
00:50:30,063 --> 00:50:33,601
Fuck's sake.
Just stay here.

751
00:50:34,669 --> 00:50:36,604
[Randall]
I just want to talk!

752
00:50:38,006 --> 00:50:40,474
Please just don't move!

753
00:50:43,678 --> 00:50:45,013
[knocking on door]

754
00:50:45,078 --> 00:50:46,313
I called the cops!

755
00:50:46,380 --> 00:50:48,215
You need to get
the fuck outta here now!

756
00:50:48,282 --> 00:50:49,751
Listen to me.

757
00:50:50,585 --> 00:50:54,121
I know it's confusing, but--
but that's not Evelyn in there.

758
00:50:54,187 --> 00:50:55,890
It's something dangerous.

759
00:50:55,957 --> 00:50:58,458
The only dangerous thing here
is you and your psycho friends!

760
00:50:58,526 --> 00:51:01,428
She killed Peter!
He's dead because of her!

761
00:51:01,495 --> 00:51:04,632
She didn't kill anybody!
She's fucking old!

762
00:51:05,800 --> 00:51:07,535
Stay the fuck back!

763
00:51:07,602 --> 00:51:09,336
[slams, locks]

764
00:51:09,403 --> 00:51:11,739
That little ivory statue
that she has,

765
00:51:11,806 --> 00:51:14,742
you're not safe as long
as that thing is in the house.

766
00:51:14,809 --> 00:51:16,578
The statue is the problem?

767
00:51:16,644 --> 00:51:19,479
It's an anchor, a vessel
for something dark.

768
00:51:19,547 --> 00:51:21,148
It's attached itself to her.

769
00:51:21,214 --> 00:51:22,850
What the fuck
are you talking about?

770
00:51:22,917 --> 00:51:26,153
It'll kill you both!
We can't leave here without--

771
00:51:26,219 --> 00:51:27,522
Okay, fine!

772
00:51:27,589 --> 00:51:29,289
If I get it for you,
will you leave?

773
00:51:29,356 --> 00:51:31,358
Yes.
That's all we want!

774
00:51:31,425 --> 00:51:33,728
Just stay outside.
I'll go get it!

775
00:51:34,261 --> 00:51:36,263
You're doing the right thing.

776
00:51:37,765 --> 00:51:41,335
[thunder rumbling]

777
00:51:42,336 --> 00:51:44,973
[Evelyn] You think you can
take this from me?

778
00:51:45,039 --> 00:51:46,273
Huh?

779
00:51:47,008 --> 00:51:50,377
[Julia]
For fuck's sake, Evelyn,
I told you to stay over there!

780
00:51:50,444 --> 00:51:51,679
Put the knife down!

781
00:51:51,746 --> 00:51:54,181
No!

782
00:51:54,181 --> 00:51:55,449
[Julia]
Please, let's talk.

783
00:51:55,516 --> 00:51:58,418
Maybe we can work
something out with them.

784
00:51:58,485 --> 00:52:00,788
Evelyn, everything's
gonna be okay.

785
00:52:00,855 --> 00:52:02,189
You're safe.
Why don't you just give me--

786
00:52:02,255 --> 00:52:05,593
No! No!

787
00:52:06,794 --> 00:52:08,796
Evelyn, stop!

788
00:52:08,863 --> 00:52:10,798
[Evelyn]
You, stop!

789
00:52:10,865 --> 00:52:12,867
Evelyn, stop.

790
00:52:16,904 --> 00:52:18,405
Where are you?

791
00:52:23,911 --> 00:52:25,780
-Fuck.
-[Evelyn laughs]

792
00:52:32,687 --> 00:52:34,589
[door creaks]

793
00:52:37,892 --> 00:52:39,426
Evelyn?

794
00:52:39,493 --> 00:52:45,700
[sinister music playing]

795
00:52:51,238 --> 00:52:52,807
Hello?

796
00:52:54,008 --> 00:52:56,878
[door creaks]

797
00:52:56,944 --> 00:53:03,283
[music continues to play]

798
00:53:20,935 --> 00:53:23,504
-[gasps]
-[Evelyn laughs]

799
00:53:23,571 --> 00:53:26,373
[footsteps thud above]

800
00:53:26,440 --> 00:53:32,647
[sinister music playing]

801
00:54:01,976 --> 00:54:04,846
[loud thuds]

802
00:54:04,912 --> 00:54:09,316
[sinister music playing]

803
00:54:14,122 --> 00:54:17,491
[thunder rumbles]

804
00:54:25,233 --> 00:54:26,934
[Randall]
Hurry up!

805
00:54:28,236 --> 00:54:29,170
Come on.

806
00:54:29,237 --> 00:54:30,805
You're here.

807
00:54:32,907 --> 00:54:36,043
We can still salvage this.
Trust me.

808
00:54:36,110 --> 00:54:37,712
Like Peter did?

809
00:54:39,346 --> 00:54:40,515
What is this?

810
00:54:40,581 --> 00:54:42,049
What are we dealing
with, Randall?

811
00:54:42,116 --> 00:54:44,018
Nothing I can't handle.

812
00:54:52,459 --> 00:54:53,761
What happened?

813
00:54:53,828 --> 00:54:57,131
We were too late.
It's already in her.

814
00:54:58,032 --> 00:55:00,935
We lost Peter,
there was nothing we could do.

815
00:55:02,369 --> 00:55:04,404
We need to get it
into the statue

816
00:55:04,471 --> 00:55:06,473
and back in here.

817
00:55:09,644 --> 00:55:13,281
Randall, this is very dangerous.

818
00:55:13,380 --> 00:55:14,882
It's not because
I'm no longer authorized.

819
00:55:14,949 --> 00:55:16,184
It's--

820
00:55:16,250 --> 00:55:19,020
You remember what happened
last time we tried this?

821
00:55:19,086 --> 00:55:21,388
You're all I've got.

822
00:55:21,454 --> 00:55:23,858
I'm not gonna lose
both of them.

823
00:55:25,126 --> 00:55:26,426
I understand.

824
00:55:26,493 --> 00:55:30,397
Randall, this one,
this one is strong.

825
00:55:30,397 --> 00:55:33,868
Stronger than anything
we ever faced before
and you know it.

826
00:55:34,401 --> 00:55:36,704
-This time is different.
-What's this?

827
00:55:36,771 --> 00:55:40,641
We can destroy it.
We only need one word.

828
00:55:40,708 --> 00:55:44,579
This is an incantation
of the blood of Christ.

829
00:55:45,680 --> 00:55:49,016
Blood of Christ.
Evelyn figured it out.

830
00:55:50,084 --> 00:55:51,953
No more hiding it away.

831
00:55:52,019 --> 00:55:55,523
I can finally make it pay
for everything that it's done.

832
00:55:55,590 --> 00:55:57,792
Send it back to hell
where it belongs.

833
00:55:57,859 --> 00:56:02,763
Hey, if this time
it doesn't work?

834
00:56:02,830 --> 00:56:05,633
We're going through the front.

835
00:56:05,700 --> 00:56:08,636
Stick together, near the back.

836
00:56:08,703 --> 00:56:12,540
Holler if you see her.

837
00:56:12,607 --> 00:56:16,644
Don't do anything
until I'm there.

838
00:56:18,012 --> 00:56:19,614
Go on.

839
00:56:21,616 --> 00:56:23,483
I'm going to fix this.

840
00:56:23,551 --> 00:56:29,757
[sinister music playing]

841
00:56:35,229 --> 00:56:37,531
She's stronger than she looks.

842
00:56:38,933 --> 00:56:42,469
If it goes south,
just run out.

843
00:56:47,041 --> 00:56:49,210
[rattling]

844
00:56:49,277 --> 00:56:52,647
Evelyn, is that you?

845
00:56:55,349 --> 00:56:58,552
[radio static]

846
00:57:01,689 --> 00:57:05,326
[Randall on recording]
<i>Honey, do you know</i>
<i>why you're here?</i>

847
00:57:06,594 --> 00:57:09,697
-[Sarah on recording]
<i>Why-- why are my hands tied?</i>
-What the hell?

848
00:57:09,764 --> 00:57:13,234
[Evelyn on recording]
<i>So you don't</i>
<i>hurt yourself again.</i>

849
00:57:13,301 --> 00:57:15,236
<i>Remember last night?</i>

850
00:57:15,303 --> 00:57:17,238
[Sarah on recording]
<i>No.</i>

851
00:57:17,305 --> 00:57:19,707
[Randall on recording]
<i>You scratched</i>
<i>until your face bled.</i>

852
00:57:19,774 --> 00:57:22,109
[Sarah on recording]
<i>Stop it.</i>

853
00:57:22,176 --> 00:57:23,744
[Sarah groans]

854
00:57:23,811 --> 00:57:25,246
[Randall on recording]
<i>How do you feel?</i>

855
00:57:25,313 --> 00:57:27,581
[Sarah on recording]
<i>My tummy really hurts.</i>

856
00:57:29,183 --> 00:57:30,718
[loud growls]

857
00:57:30,785 --> 00:57:33,521
[Sarah on recording]
<i>I don't feel good.</i>

858
00:57:33,521 --> 00:57:36,190
[Evelyn on recording]
<i>Do you remember</i>
<i>when we went on the dig?</i>

859
00:57:39,126 --> 00:57:41,028
<i>Do you remember</i>
<i>what school you go to?</i>

860
00:57:41,095 --> 00:57:44,031
[Sarah on recording]
<i>No! No!</i>

861
00:57:44,098 --> 00:57:46,367
[Evelyn on recording]
<i>What do you remember?</i>

862
00:57:46,434 --> 00:57:47,868
[Sarah on recording]
<i>No. Mommy!</i>

863
00:57:47,935 --> 00:57:50,004
[Evelyn on recording]
<i>Sarah?</i>

864
00:57:50,071 --> 00:57:52,073
[Sarah on recording]
<i>I pray the soul</i>
<i>is another body to take.</i>

865
00:57:52,139 --> 00:57:54,408
<i>I only remember</i>
<i>that you're a shit mother!</i>

866
00:57:54,542 --> 00:57:55,910
<i>-</i> [Randall on recording]
<i>Sarah!</i>
<i>-</i> [slapping sound]

867
00:57:55,977 --> 00:57:57,144
[Evelyn on recording]
<i>Randall!</i>

868
00:57:57,211 --> 00:57:58,546
[evil laugh]

869
00:57:58,612 --> 00:58:00,314
[Evelyn on recording]
<i>Oh, my God.</i>

870
00:58:00,381 --> 00:58:01,916
[Sarah on recording]
<i>Is that all you've got,</i>
<i>old man?</i>

871
00:58:01,983 --> 00:58:03,551
<i>-Hmm?</i>
-[Sarah laughs]

872
00:58:03,551 --> 00:58:04,952
[Evelyn on recording]
<i>Stop it!</i>

873
00:58:05,019 --> 00:58:06,554
[Sarah on recording]
<i>No!</i>

874
00:58:06,587 --> 00:58:07,722
[Evelyn on recording]
<i>Look at her!</i>

875
00:58:07,788 --> 00:58:09,190
[Sarah on recording]
<i>No!</i>

876
00:58:09,256 --> 00:58:10,391
[Evelyn on recording]
<i>What have we done?</i>

877
00:58:10,458 --> 00:58:12,727
[loud scream]

878
00:58:14,962 --> 00:58:16,764
Shit.

879
00:58:21,936 --> 00:58:24,572
[glass shatters in distance]

880
00:58:33,147 --> 00:58:34,281
[knife clangs]

881
00:58:34,348 --> 00:58:40,588
[sinister music playing]

882
00:58:56,971 --> 00:58:59,407
Evelyn, where have you been?

883
00:58:59,473 --> 00:59:01,609
[Evelyn] Why do you have that?

884
00:59:02,877 --> 00:59:04,879
You're scaring me.

885
00:59:06,213 --> 00:59:08,215
Please don't hurt me.

886
00:59:10,618 --> 00:59:12,987
[voice deepening]
Why are you following me?

887
00:59:13,954 --> 00:59:18,292
[Julia]
I was looking for you.
Where were you?

888
00:59:19,326 --> 00:59:21,530
Do you remember anything?

889
00:59:21,629 --> 00:59:24,932
I remember some things.

890
00:59:26,100 --> 00:59:28,903
I had a dream about my mother,

891
00:59:29,904 --> 00:59:33,040
not long after she passed.

892
00:59:33,107 --> 00:59:36,944
We were making dinner together,
like every other night.

893
00:59:37,011 --> 00:59:39,847
And right in the middle,
she stopped

894
00:59:39,914 --> 00:59:41,682
and said she had to go.

895
00:59:41,749 --> 00:59:46,720
So I ran after her
to say goodbye,

896
00:59:47,955 --> 00:59:52,059
but she kept walking
like she didn't hear me.

897
00:59:52,126 --> 00:59:55,863
So I followed her,
but she was lost,

898
00:59:55,930 --> 01:00:00,067
disappeared into the fog.
[echoing]

899
01:00:00,134 --> 01:00:02,970
[sniffling]

900
01:00:03,037 --> 01:00:07,842
How do you know that?
I never told you that.

901
01:00:18,252 --> 01:00:22,490
[Evelyn laughs]

902
01:00:22,557 --> 01:00:25,426
[thunder booming]

903
01:00:25,493 --> 01:00:31,699
[sinister music playing]

904
01:00:47,181 --> 01:00:49,116
[Evelyn laughs]

905
01:00:49,183 --> 01:00:51,986
[Evelyn]
I never told you that.

906
01:00:54,221 --> 01:00:58,826
Evelyn?
Stop, you're freaking me out.

907
01:01:06,800 --> 01:01:12,773
[Julia's Mom]
Jules? Jules.

908
01:01:18,045 --> 01:01:19,813
Mom?

909
01:01:27,121 --> 01:01:30,157
[Julia's Mom]
Can you come here, please?

910
01:01:33,562 --> 01:01:35,863
I missed you, <i>mija.</i>

911
01:01:35,930 --> 01:01:37,765
This can't...

912
01:01:37,765 --> 01:01:39,867
[Julia's Mom]
The last time I saw you
was at the airport.

913
01:01:39,934 --> 01:01:44,573
We were saying goodbye
and the sunlight
was shining behind you.

914
01:01:44,639 --> 01:01:46,974
-And it was so beautiful.
-[Julia] You're not my mom.

915
01:01:47,041 --> 01:01:48,943
[Julia's Mom] Oh, Jules,

916
01:01:49,009 --> 01:01:53,480
remember when you were five
and broke your arm?

917
01:01:53,548 --> 01:01:57,351
-Who fed you every meal?
-No. Stop it. Stop it.
Please, stop.

918
01:01:57,418 --> 01:01:59,554
[Julia's Mom]
When you were 12 and missed
a month of school

919
01:01:59,621 --> 01:02:03,791
with pneumonia,
who nursed you back to health?

920
01:02:03,824 --> 01:02:05,926
Who cried with you
when your prom date

921
01:02:05,993 --> 01:02:07,795
didn't show up?

922
01:02:07,795 --> 01:02:11,232
-I held you. I comforted you.
-Stop.

923
01:02:11,298 --> 01:02:13,635
-[Julia's Mom]
I was there for you.
<i>-No puedo...</i>

924
01:02:13,702 --> 01:02:16,503
-[Julia's Mom]
It's so cold here.
-Stop it.

925
01:02:16,571 --> 01:02:19,340
[Julia's Mom] Please.
Let me see you again.

926
01:02:19,406 --> 01:02:21,809
I said stop it!

927
01:02:24,378 --> 01:02:26,514
<i>Te quiero, mija.</i>

928
01:02:26,581 --> 01:02:28,449
-[screams]
-[Evelyn laughs]

929
01:02:28,516 --> 01:02:31,519
[body thuds]

930
01:02:32,886 --> 01:02:35,055
[Julia groans]

931
01:02:36,056 --> 01:02:42,263
[sinister music playing]

932
01:02:53,907 --> 01:02:57,111
[screams]

933
01:03:00,381 --> 01:03:01,382
Okay.

934
01:03:01,448 --> 01:03:03,417
Okay.

935
01:03:06,320 --> 01:03:09,323
[crying]

936
01:03:14,428 --> 01:03:16,964
Oh, okay.

937
01:03:20,334 --> 01:03:23,337
[groans]

938
01:03:26,040 --> 01:03:27,374
[lock rattling]

939
01:03:27,441 --> 01:03:28,876
Okay.

940
01:03:34,649 --> 01:03:37,117
[panting]

941
01:03:37,184 --> 01:03:38,553
Okay.

942
01:03:46,695 --> 01:03:50,998
Oh, what is this?

943
01:03:51,065 --> 01:03:57,271
[sinister music playing]

944
01:04:07,114 --> 01:04:08,916
What is this?

945
01:04:08,949 --> 01:04:15,155
[music continues to play]

946
01:04:30,705 --> 01:04:33,575
[thunder roars]

947
01:04:33,641 --> 01:04:39,647
[sinister music playing]

948
01:04:46,453 --> 01:04:48,188
-[glass shattering]
-[Randall] Evelyn!

949
01:04:48,255 --> 01:04:50,190
[Evelyn] Way too late.
Time's over.

950
01:04:50,257 --> 01:04:52,159
[Randall]
Edgar, hold her!

951
01:04:53,561 --> 01:04:54,696
Please, hear us!

952
01:04:54,763 --> 01:04:56,497
[Evelyn]
Nobody's listening!

953
01:04:56,564 --> 01:04:59,567
[indiscernible speech]

954
01:05:01,068 --> 01:05:03,470
[Evelyn laughs]

955
01:05:03,538 --> 01:05:05,272
[Randall]
Surrender her! Don't listen.

956
01:05:05,339 --> 01:05:07,776
By the power of God,
surrender her.

957
01:05:07,842 --> 01:05:10,812
[Evelyn]
You don't stand a chance!

958
01:05:10,879 --> 01:05:14,081
[indiscernible speech]

959
01:05:16,250 --> 01:05:19,821
Oh, shit. Fuck!
I don't have my keys.

960
01:05:19,888 --> 01:05:21,288
I don't have my keys.

961
01:05:21,355 --> 01:05:23,290
-[loud growls]
-[glass shatters]

962
01:05:23,357 --> 01:05:24,491
[Randall]
Oh, huh, wait!

963
01:05:24,559 --> 01:05:26,093
[Evelyn grunts]

964
01:05:26,160 --> 01:05:28,696
Just get your fucking keys
and get outta here.

965
01:05:28,763 --> 01:05:31,699
[indistinct speech]

966
01:05:31,766 --> 01:05:36,638
[Randall]
Oh, God, thrust into Hell
Satan and all evil spirits

967
01:05:36,704 --> 01:05:40,909
who wander through the world
for the ruin of souls.

968
01:05:41,008 --> 01:05:42,042
Amen.

969
01:05:42,109 --> 01:05:43,511
[Evelyn]
Stupid priest.

970
01:05:43,578 --> 01:05:46,113
[Randall]
Evelyn, stop.
Be careful!

971
01:05:46,180 --> 01:05:47,481
[Evelyn]
Get outta here!

972
01:05:47,549 --> 01:05:50,017
Evelyn, fight it.
I know you can.

973
01:05:50,017 --> 01:05:54,021
In the name of God, the Father,
Jesus Christ the Son,

974
01:05:54,087 --> 01:05:56,925
and by the power
of the Holy Spirit,

975
01:05:57,024 --> 01:05:59,259
you will obey me,
you foul thing.

976
01:05:59,326 --> 01:06:03,631
God cast you into a pit
of hellfire, into that pit
you shall return.

977
01:06:03,698 --> 01:06:07,334
Oh, I can already
feel her suffering.

978
01:06:07,401 --> 01:06:09,470
Evelyn is stronger
than you will ever be.

979
01:06:09,537 --> 01:06:11,873
That's not
who I'm talking about.

980
01:06:11,940 --> 01:06:15,275
Your daughter
is in eternal torture,
because of you.

981
01:06:15,342 --> 01:06:19,848
You failed her, but I,
I can bring her peace.

982
01:06:19,914 --> 01:06:21,215
[speaks foreign language]

983
01:06:21,281 --> 01:06:22,784
-Don't listen to it.
-[Evelyn laughs]

984
01:06:22,851 --> 01:06:24,552
Leave the flesh
of God's righteous creature

985
01:06:24,619 --> 01:06:28,590
and return to the darkness
from whence you came!

986
01:06:28,656 --> 01:06:33,427
Ah, your souls or hers!

987
01:06:33,494 --> 01:06:38,867
-Little Sarah's blossoming
into a lovely woman.
-Shut your mouth, demon!

988
01:06:38,933 --> 01:06:42,069
Oh, you should be honored
to have made

989
01:06:42,135 --> 01:06:44,271
such a precious sacrifice
for me.

990
01:06:44,338 --> 01:06:47,174
I have them both now,
and Evelyn has given up

991
01:06:47,241 --> 01:06:50,177
her defiance
and replaced it with screams.

992
01:06:50,244 --> 01:06:52,079
It's a sweet symphony!

993
01:06:52,145 --> 01:06:53,180
Evie, fight it.

994
01:06:53,247 --> 01:06:55,215
You're stronger than this thing.

995
01:06:55,282 --> 01:06:57,685
You told me that you
found a way and you did.

996
01:06:57,752 --> 01:07:00,187
But I need your help,
so fight it.

997
01:07:00,254 --> 01:07:02,790
Fight it for her!
Fight it for all of us!

998
01:07:04,626 --> 01:07:07,494
The blood of Christ
seals the cage.

999
01:07:07,562 --> 01:07:11,533
By all that's holy in the power
of the Kingdom of Heaven,

1000
01:07:11,599 --> 01:07:16,004
I banish you!
Return to your prison.

1001
01:07:16,103 --> 01:07:17,605
[groans]

1002
01:07:17,672 --> 01:07:19,574
Your soul's it is.

1003
01:07:19,641 --> 01:07:22,242
[screams]

1004
01:07:22,309 --> 01:07:23,443
[flesh ripping]

1005
01:07:23,511 --> 01:07:26,246
[screams]

1006
01:07:26,313 --> 01:07:32,252
[sinister music playing]

1007
01:07:32,319 --> 01:07:36,123
[screams and flesh ripping
continue]

1008
01:07:48,302 --> 01:07:51,338
[loud screeches]

1009
01:07:51,405 --> 01:07:54,441
[crying]

1010
01:07:56,611 --> 01:07:58,680
Make it stop.

1011
01:07:59,914 --> 01:08:04,752
[screaming]

1012
01:08:04,819 --> 01:08:09,824
[sinister music playing]

1013
01:08:17,632 --> 01:08:20,668
[thunder roaring]

1014
01:08:20,735 --> 01:08:23,571
[panting]

1015
01:08:23,638 --> 01:08:25,305
[keys jingle]

1016
01:08:25,372 --> 01:08:28,576
[Julia sobbing]

1017
01:08:51,866 --> 01:08:57,872
[sinister music playing]

1018
01:09:36,911 --> 01:09:41,916
[music continues to play]

1019
01:09:48,056 --> 01:09:51,425
[whimpers]

1020
01:09:57,565 --> 01:09:59,867
What have you done, Evelyn?

1021
01:09:59,934 --> 01:10:04,271
[sinister music playing]

1022
01:10:09,811 --> 01:10:10,578
[gasps]

1023
01:10:10,645 --> 01:10:12,580
[Randall]
You can't leave.

1024
01:10:12,647 --> 01:10:14,515
We need to get you
to a hospital.

1025
01:10:14,582 --> 01:10:16,017
Come on, let's get you
to my car.

1026
01:10:16,084 --> 01:10:17,350
I can't.

1027
01:10:17,417 --> 01:10:20,888
Just try
or you'll bleed to death.

1028
01:10:20,955 --> 01:10:22,489
Please, help me save her.

1029
01:10:22,557 --> 01:10:24,892
What is wrong with you people?

1030
01:10:24,959 --> 01:10:26,728
When this is over, bury it.

1031
01:10:26,794 --> 01:10:27,962
What?

1032
01:10:28,029 --> 01:10:31,599
When everything is done,
put it in the ground.

1033
01:10:31,666 --> 01:10:33,735
It's just like in the basement.

1034
01:10:33,801 --> 01:10:35,670
Like, what these?

1035
01:10:36,871 --> 01:10:37,872
Yeah.

1036
01:10:37,939 --> 01:10:39,073
And then-- and then--
and then,

1037
01:10:39,140 --> 01:10:40,708
there were these letters.

1038
01:10:40,775 --> 01:10:43,711
E-L-I-M.

1039
01:10:44,779 --> 01:10:46,013
Elim.

1040
01:10:47,014 --> 01:10:49,150
What does it mean?

1041
01:10:49,217 --> 01:10:50,752
We need to hurry.

1042
01:10:50,818 --> 01:10:52,352
[grunts]

1043
01:10:52,419 --> 01:10:54,055
No. No, please, let me go.

1044
01:10:54,122 --> 01:10:55,923
You can't go.

1045
01:10:55,990 --> 01:10:58,226
My dad needs me.

1046
01:10:58,291 --> 01:11:01,495
Don't let Evelyn die alone.

1047
